$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=g3t7  LOC_AFTER=?

* A substitution that changes both the range and the body of a finite sum: ` sumeq12dv ` has no ` s ` variant, so tools/congr.py lifts its body hypothesis with ` adantr ` .

s1::id |- ( f = N -> f = N )
c1:s1:oveq2d |- ( f = N -> ( 1 ... f ) = ( 1 ... N ) )
c2:s1:oveq2d |- ( f = N -> ( j x. f ) = ( j x. N ) )
c3:c2:adantr |- ( ( f = N /\ j e. ( 1 ... f ) ) -> ( j x. f ) = ( j x. N ) )
qed:c1,c3:sumeq12dv |- ( f = N -> sum_ j e. ( 1 ... f ) ( j x. f ) = sum_ j e. ( 1 ... N ) ( j x. N ) )
